# Part 8 - User Preferences Table, Insights Table, Database Summary

# 22. Table — User Preferences

---

# 22.1 Purpose

The `user_preferences` table stores personalized application settings for each user.

Unlike the `profiles` table, which stores user identity information, this table manages configurable application behavior, AI preferences, interface customization, and future personalization settings.

Keeping preferences separate from profile information allows application settings to evolve independently without affecting authentication or user identity.

Each authenticated user has exactly one preferences record.

---

# 22.2 Relationships

```text
profiles

│

│ 1 : 1

▼

user_preferences
```

Each profile owns exactly one preference record.

Preferences cannot exist without an associated profile.

---

