---

# 23.10 Design Decisions

## Why Store Insights Separately?

Insights are long-lived AI artifacts rather than conversational responses.

Separating them enables independent generation, management, bookmarking, and future analytics.

---

## Why Store Source References?

Every insight maintains traceability by referencing the supporting documents and chunks used during generation.

This improves explainability and user trust.

---

## Why Generate Insights Asynchronously?

Insight generation can be computationally expensive.

Running it in the background prevents delays during uploads and conversations while keeping the user experience responsive.

---

# 23.11 Business Rules

- Every insight belongs to exactly one authenticated user.
- Insights are generated only from documents the user owns.
- Source references are preserved for every generated insight.
- Users may bookmark insights for future reference.
- Deleted documents are excluded from future insight generation.
- Insights generated from deleted documents may be regenerated or removed during background maintenance.

---

