# 24.4 Database Design Principles

The KnowledgeOS database architecture follows several core engineering principles.

### Single Source of Truth

Every entity has one authoritative storage location.

---

### Strong Referential Integrity

All relationships are protected through foreign keys and database constraints.

---

### User Isolation

Every record belongs to a single authenticated user.

Queries are always scoped using the user's profile identifier.

---

### Soft Deletion

Critical user data follows a multi-stage deletion lifecycle.

Soft-deleted records remain recoverable during the retention period while becoming immediately invisible to retrieval.

---

### Immutable Knowledge

Document chunks and AI-generated messages are immutable.

Updates generate new versions rather than modifying existing records.

---

### Separation of Concerns

Transactional data remains inside PostgreSQL.

Semantic retrieval remains inside ChromaDB.

Each system performs the task for which it is best suited.

---

### Future Scalability

The schema has been designed to accommodate:

- Knowledge Graphs
- Voice AI
- OCR
- Hybrid Search
- Team Workspaces
- Plugin Ecosystem
- Multiple LLM Providers
- Multi-modal Knowledge
- Advanced Analytics

without requiring structural redesign.

